Embedded React: a radial gradient seen through a View's border ring.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/include/er_scene.h,
engine/scene/er_node_internal.h, engine/scene/compositor.c,
engine/rendering/border_sweep.c, engine/rendering/border_sweep.h,
bridges/quickjs/native_ui_bridge.c and
bridges/quickjs/js/src/embedded-react/index.d.ts. Proposed upstream, with the
other border ring patches, as pull request #325.

Magic UI's ShineBorder is a CSS radial-gradient on a background several times
the box, its position looping corner to corner, masked to the border. The View
style borderGradient {type: 'radial', width, size, stops} draws it in the same
ring as the conic border gradient: an ellipse farthest-corner gradient on a
background `size` times the box. borderGradientAngle drives the loop on the
native driver: one 360-degree turn takes background-position from 0% 0% to
100% 100% at 180 and back, so a linear Animated loop of 0 to 360 is the CSS
keyframes.

